/* loadscreen.cpp -- small loading screen shown while Render_Init() loads the
 * hundreds of textures (instead of a long black screen).
 *
 * Everything (background, logo, soil strip, grass strip, sprouts) is embedded
 * in this file, so nothing needs to be on the SD card / disc to see it, and no
 * header has to be replaced. Cut from the user's artwork.
 *
 * Layout (640x480): background art, logo at the top, a soil strip with a grass
 * strip on its top edge that is revealed from left to right as loading
 * progresses, and a sprout that pops up and is bigger at every quarter
 * (25 %, 50 %, 75 %, 100 %) of the total loading work.
 *
 * Used by Render_Init():  Loading_Set(0..1) after every loaded item,
 * Loading_Finish() when done (frees the textures). */
